Refactor this Go function so it respects context cancellation and returns an error instead of panicking:

```go
func FetchAll(urls []string) []string {
    var out []string
    for _, u := range urls {
        resp, err := http.Get(u)
        if err != nil { panic(err) }
        b, _ := io.ReadAll(resp.Body)
        out = append(out, string(b))
    }
    return out
}
```
Fetch the URLs concurrently with a limit of 4 in flight.
